cms/ holds files from the CMS Home Health PC Pricer for calendar year 2021,
as the U.S. Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services publishes them: the
calculator HHCAL213 and the driver, manager and opener that call it
(hhcal213.cbl, hhdrv213.cbl, hhmgr213.cbl, hhopn213.cbl), the copybooks
they use, and the test claims and tables shipped with them (HHAFILE,
MSAFILE, CBSAFILE, HRGTABL, REVTABL). They are CMS's, unmodified; verify.sh
makes its two build-only changes to copies in work/.

cocoon/hhdrv213_tap.cbl is CMS's driver, hhdrv213.cbl, with Cocoon's tap
added: statements that print, as hex, every record passed to HHCAL213
before and after each call.

cms/esrd/ holds files from the CMS ESRD mainframe pricing programs for
calendar year 2021 (CY2021.2), as CMS publishes them: the 20 calculators
ESCAL056 to ESCAL212 and the copybooks they use (BILLCPY, RTCCPY, WAGECPY). They are CMS's, unmodified.

cocoon/esrd/<PROGRAM>_direct_tap.cbl is a short driver written by Cocoon's
harness for that calculator, not a CMS file, with Cocoon's tap added; the
untapped driver is more/esrd/<PROGRAM>_direct.cbl.

cms/ltch/ holds files from the CMS LTCH mainframe pricing programs for
fiscal year 2021 (FY2021.2), as CMS publishes them: the 28 calculators
LTCAL032 to LTCAL212 and the copybooks they use (BLEND152, IPDRG063, IPDRG071, IPDRG080, IPDRG090, IPDRG104, IPDRG110, IPDRG123, IPDRG130, IPDRG141, IPDRG152, IPDRG160, IPDRG170, IPDRG181, IPDRG190, IPDRG200, IPDRG211, IRFBN091, IRFBN102, IRFBN105, LTDRG031, LTDRG041, LTDRG057, LTDRG062, LTDRG075, LTDRG080, LTDRG086, LTDRG093, LTDRG095, LTDRG100, LTDRG110, LTDRG123, LTDRG130, LTDRG141, LTDRG152, LTDRG160, LTDRG170, LTDRG181, LTDRG190, LTDRG200, LTDRG210). They are CMS's, unmodified, each
identical byte for byte to its member of CMS's fy20212-ltch-mainframe-pricing-programs.zip; cms/ltch/build/ holds build-only copies of the 23 calculators from
LTCAL063 on, with REDEFINES clauses changed as the README says.

cocoon/ltch/<PROGRAM>_direct_tap.cbl is a short driver written by Cocoon's
harness for that calculator, not a CMS file, with Cocoon's tap added; the
untapped driver is more/ltch/<PROGRAM>_direct.cbl.
